# Merge drivers for the files a wave touches most.
#
# WHY
#
# The string catalog is the most-touched file in a wave (4 cards on the
# current board, 7 touches inside a 12-commit window on main). Its keys are
# NOT sorted: a new key lands in the MIDDLE of the file. So two cards that
# each add a DIFFERENT key produce a textual conflict under git's normal
# merge, because both insertions land in the same neighbourhood.
#
# Measured: `git merge-tree` on two branches that each added one distinct
# key returned CONFLICT.
#
# The driver merges the catalog at the KEY level instead, so that class of
# collision does not happen. A genuine disagreement (the same key, two
# different values) still conflicts, and the driver NAMES the key, so the
# human resolves a string instead of hunting a marker in a 6400-line file.
#
# The driver path is repo-relative: git runs a merge driver from the top of
# the working tree. The matching config lives in .git/config (a local
# setting, so it is not part of this file) and is installed by
# Scripts/setup-dev-env.sh.
*.xcstrings merge=xcstrings
